    "user_request_original": "Design a 20-layer alternating MgF2/HfO2 planar multilayer filter on fused silica substrate for normal incidence. Initialize layer thicknesses using geometric progression with ratio r sampled uniformly from [1.08, 1.12] for both MgF2 and HfO2 layers. Enforce hard upper bound of 85nm on all HfO2 layer thicknesses during initialization and optimization. MgF2 layers may range 20-200nm. Evaluate coherent S-matrix transmittance spectrum from 255-1100nm. Score three objectives: mean transmittance maximization in 255-280nm passband, mean transmittance minimization in 300-700nm visible stopband, mean transmittance minimization in 700-1100nm NIR stopband. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with bound projection. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 255–280 nm; low transmittance in 300–700 nm; low transmittance in 700–1100 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 300–700 nm; transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30; no metal layers; conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials only.",
